SUMMARY:LIVE: MOOR MOTHER ☓ FETISH BONES // ROJIN SHARAFI (IR/A) (Uhrzeit prüfen)
LOCATION:Flucc
DESCRIPTION:@DECK | MOOR MOTHER ☓ FETISH BONES 10TH ANNIVERSARY TOUR First released September 16\, 2016\, Fetish Bones was the debut album of Philadelphia based musician\, artist\, and activist Camae Ayewa\, performing as Moor Mother. Recorded in her home studio using a collection of machines\, field recordings\, and analog noisemakers\, the album's 13 tracks fused the visceral anger of punk with the expansive improvisatory spirit of Sun Ra\, arriving not as a way to forget but as a demand to remember. The record was named an Album of the Year by The Wire and Jazz Right Now\, and landed on Pitchfork's Best Experimental LPs of 2016\, Rolling Stone's Best Avant Albums of 2016\, and Thump's 25 Best Experimental Albums of 2016. "Deadbeat Protest" made both Pitchfork's and Noisey's Best Songs of 2016 lists\, and Bandcamp named Ayewa its 2016 Artist of the Year while including Fetish Bones among its 100 Best Records of 2016. Ten years later\, Don Giovanni Records celebrates that debut with a 10th anniversary edition\, pressed with a foil album cover and featuring the previously unreleased bonus track "Marian Anderson\," a collaboration with Wolf Weston and Wooden Elephant. In the years since Fetish Bones\, Ayewa has become one of experimental music's most celebrated and prolific voices. Since her debut\, Ayewa’s work has been featured at the Guggenheim Museum\, The Met\, Carnegie Mellon and Carnegie Hall\, Documenta 15\, the Berlin Jazz Festival\, and the Glastonbury Festival. She has been named a Pew Fellow\, a Kitchen Inaugural Emerging Artist Awardee\, a Leeway Transformation Award\, a Blade of Grass Fellow as part of Black Quantum Futurism\, and a Rad Girls Philly Artist of the Year. She has also been featured as an Artist-in-Residence at West Philadelphia Neighborhood Time Exchange\, WORM! Rotterdam residency\, and the Creative Capital and CERN collide residency with Black Quantum Futurism.  Rojin Sharafi is a Tehran-born\, Vienna-based sound artist\, composer\, and performer working across electroacoustic music\, noise\, and experimental electronics. Her visceral sonic language blends analog\, acoustic\, and digital tools\, exploring tension\, rupture\, and transformation. Praised by The Wire for her “thrilling\, variegated” sound world\, Sharafi’s latest album O.O.Orifice follows critically acclaimed releases including Urns Waiting to be Fed (2019)\, Zangaar (2020)\, and Kariz (2021). She also performs with the folk futurist ensemble HUUUM. Her work has been presented internationally\, from London to New York\, affirming her as a vital voice in experimental music. ------   VvK 25.- AK 30.- 
URL:https://flucc.at/events/FfyaLS-live-moor-mother-fetish-bones-10th-anniversary-tour-rojin-sharafi-ira/
